```java
public static boolean isOxymoron(String string) {
    String[] words = string.split(" ");
    int count = words.length;
    for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {
        for (int j = i + 1; j < count; j++) {
            if (words[i].equals(words[j])) {
                return true;
            }
        }
    }
    return false;
}
public static void main(String[] args) {
    String string = "bittersweet";
    if (isOxymoron(string)) {
        System.out.println(string + " is an oxymoron");
    } else {
        System.out.println(string + " is not an oxymoron");
    }
}
```
This code splits the string into individual words using the `split()` function and then checks if any two words are the same. If they are, then the string is considered an oxymoron.

