1. Quantity Discount: This is a discount that applies when a customer purchases a certain quantity of a product. For example, if a customer purchases 5 or more 11-inch iPad Pros that cost more than $500 each, they get a 20% discount on the total cost.
2. Bulk Discount: This is a discount that applies when a customer purchases a certain quantity of a product. For example, if a customer purchases 3 or more Smart Keyboard Folios that cost more than $100 each, they get a 10% discount on the total cost.
3. No Discount: If the customer purchases less than the quantity required for a discount or the price of the product is less than the minimum price required for a discount, then no discount is applied.

