```
Once you have a private/public key pair, you can use it to sign and verify data using blockchain technology. For example, if you're using the Ethereum blockchain, you can use the Web3Swift library to sign and verify transactions:
```swift
import Web3Swift
let privateKeyData = privateKey.rawRepresentation
let signer = EthECDSASigner(privateKey: privateKeyData)
let transaction = EthSendTransaction(
    from: "0x...",
    to: "0x...",
    value: EthNumber(value: 1, unit: .eth),
    gasPrice: EthNumber(value: 10, unit: .gwei),
    gas: EthNumber(value: 21000),
