The pattern in the sequence of numbers is that each row represents a different mathematical operation applied to the previous number in the sequence. The first row represents the initial sequence of numbers. The second row represents the sequence after adding 2 to each number in the initial sequence. The third row represents the sequence after multiplying each number in the initial sequence by the corresponding number in the second row. The fourth row represents the sequence after subtracting 2 from each number in the third row. The fifth row represents the sequence after dividing each number in the third row by the corresponding number in the initial sequence.
A mathematical formula to generate the sequence is:
n = 2
